title: v0.4.0: validator fixes and runtime hardening
---
date: 2026-04-09
---
author: Labyricorn
---
summary: A false-positive validator rule, Windows path handling, stricter API methods, and parse-once control extraction.
---
tags: architecture, configuration, html
---
source_commit: c78872fc6067a5ecdb5b08d574037b535325259e
---
body:

The v0.4.0 pair of releases focused on correctness and stability.

**Validator.** The first release fixed a rule that wrongly required
`data-tf-bind` on any element carrying `data-tf-label`. Fire buttons legitimately
pair a label with `data-tf-fire`, and the mismatch produced fourteen false errors
across two starter packs. The validator now distinguishes bindings from fire
buttons. A second fix builds required-file paths with `filepath.Join`, so the
checks work on Windows.

**Runtime API.** Control endpoints now require `POST`, with `OPTIONS` allowed for
CORS preflight, while parameters are still read through `FormValue`, which
accepts both query strings and form bodies. Assets are served from both
`/assets/...` and the documented `/?path=assets/...` form, resolving from the
pack root.

**Stability.** Control parsing used to mutate shared element structs from several
request paths, which risked data races. Bindings, CSS variables, and fire events
are now parsed once at scan time, and handlers no longer mutate elements. Live
control state resets on a pack reload, matching the documented behavior of
ephemeral session state.

This entry was written from the project's changelog.

[Commit c78872f](https://github.com/Labyricorn/TitleFlow/commit/c78872fc6067a5ecdb5b08d574037b535325259e)
